468
00:49:38.270 --> 00:49:52.570
Audio shared by Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): We all live inside many different governance ecosystems, even if we don't think of them that way. We follow laws, watch sports where players obey the rules, and buy products that meet safety standards. These systems give us fairness and trust.

469
00:49:52.620 --> 00:50:01.480
Audio shared by Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): But how do these rules get created? Governance requirements usually come from four ideas. Risk, mandate, suitability, and leverage.

